"📏 <b>Limits</b>\n<blockquote>Telegram sets most of these, not Rumi ✨</blockquote>\n\n• A text message holds up to 4096 characters\n• A photo or video caption is usually up to 1024 characters\n• A message can carry up to 100 buttons, 8 per row\n• Note names are cut at 50 characters\n\n<blockquote>If a long note fails to send, split it into two notes 💫</blockquote>": "",
"🔐 <b>Privacy</b>\n<blockquote>Here is what Rumi keeps so its features can work ✨</blockquote>\n\n• Your Telegram id, first name and username, for your wallet and rankings\n• Each group's settings, notes, filters, warns and rules\n• Short AI chat memory for the chat where you talk to Rumi\n\nRumi never asks for your phone number or passwords.\n<blockquote>Want your data removed? Ask the bot owner 💫</blockquote>": "",
"🖋️ <b>Formatting guide</b>\n<blockquote>Rumi reads these tags in notes, filters and welcome texts ✨</blockquote>\n\n&lt;b&gt;bold&lt;/b&gt; → <b>bold</b>\n&lt;i&gt;italic&lt;/i&gt; → <i>italic</i>\n&lt;u&gt;underline&lt;/u&gt; → <u>underline</u>\n&lt;s&gt;strike&lt;/s&gt; → <s>strike</s>\n&lt;code&gt;code&lt;/code&gt; → <code>code</code>\n&lt;tg-spoiler&gt;secret&lt;/tg-spoiler&gt; → <tg-spoiler>secret</tg-spoiler>\n&lt;a href=\"https://example.com\"&gt;link&lt;/a&gt; → <a href=\"https://example.com\">link</a>\n&lt;blockquote&gt;quote&lt;/blockquote&gt; → quote box\n\n<blockquote>Buttons, fillings and tags are explained in /help → Notes 💫</blockquote>": "",
