"🛡️ <b>Moderation</b>\n<blockquote>Pick a topic to see how each command works.\nBlue = topics, green = back, red = close 💫</blockquote>": "",
"Admins only. Reply to someone, or use @username / user ID.\n\n/ban /unban\n/mute /unmute\n/kick\n/tban 2h and /tmute 30m: timed (s, m, h, d, w)\n/dban /dmute /dkick: also deletes their message\n/sban /smute /skick: silent, your command disappears\n/kickme: leave the group yourself\n\nExample: /tmute @user 2h spamming\nMost actions come with an undo button.": "",
"/warn reason: add a warning\n/dwarn: warn and delete their message\n/swarn: silent warn\n/warns: see someone's warnings\n/rmwarn: remove the latest one\n/resetwarn: clear one person\n/resetallwarns: clear everyone\n\nSettings (per group):\n/warnlimit 5\n/warnmode ban, mute, kick, tban or tmute (example: /warnmode tmute 6h)\n/warntime 4w (or off): warnings expire\n/warnings: see your settings": "",
"/purge: reply to the first message, I delete everything down to now\n/purge 20: reply to a message, I delete 20 from there\n/spurge: same, no confirmation message\n/del: reply to one message to remove it\n/purgefrom then /purgeto: mark the start, then reply to the end\n\nI need the Delete messages permission. Telegram only lets me remove messages from the last 48 hours.": "",
"Approved users skip locks, blocklists and flood checks.\n\n/approve: reply or @username\n/unapprove\n/approved: list everyone\n/unapproveall\n/approval: check someone's status": "",
"Locked things get deleted for normal members. Admins and approved users are exempt.\n\n/lock sticker photo: lock one or more types\n/unlock sticker\n/locks: see what is locked\n/locktypes: every lock type\n/lockwarns on: breaking a lock adds a warning\n\nCustom punishment: /lock invitelink ### no ads {ban}\nReset it: /lock invitelink ###\n\nAllowlist: /allowlist @channel or a link, /rmallowlist, /rmallowlistall": "",
"Messages with blocklisted words get deleted.\n\n/addblocklist word reason\n/addblocklist \"a sentence\" reason\n/addblocklist (hi, hey) reason: several at once\n/rmblocklist word\n/blocklist\n\nWildcards: ? one character, * a run of characters, ** anything\nPrefixes: exact:hi and prefix:hi\n\nSettings: /blocklistmode warn (or ban, mute, kick, tban, tmute)\n/blocklistdelete on or off\n/setblocklistreason text\n\nPer word: /addblocklist boo Scary {tmute 6h} or {warn} {nodel}": "",
"Stops people sending too many messages too fast.\n\n/flood: see your settings\n/setflood 7: trigger after 7 messages\n/setfloodtimer 10 30s: 10 messages within 30 seconds\n/setfloodtimer off\n/floodmode ban, mute, kick, tban or tmute (example: /floodmode tmute 3h)\n/clearflood on: also delete the flood messages\n\nAdmins and approved users are never affected.": "",
"During a raid, every new member is temp-banned.\n\n/antiraid: switch on (or /antiraid 3h for a set time)\n/antiraid off\n/raidtime 6h: how long raid mode lasts\n/raidactiontime 1h: how long joiners are banned\n/autoantiraid 15: starts by itself if 15 people join in a minute\n/autoantiraid off": "",
"/rules: read the group rules\n/setrules text: set them (admins)\n/resetrules\n/privaterules on: /rules is sent to their PM\n/setrulesbutton text and /resetrulesbutton: name of the rules button": "",
"Members can call the admins to a bad message.\n\nReply to the message with /report or @admin\n/reports on or off (admins)\n\nAdmins cannot report, and admins cannot be reported.": "",
"/pin: reply to a message (add loud to notify everyone)\n/permapin text: I send and pin your text\n/unpin: reply to unpin one, or unpins the latest\n/unpinall\n/pinned: jump to the pinned message\n/antichannelpin on: undo Telegram's auto-pin of channel posts\n/cleanlinked on: delete posts from the linked channel": "",
"/welcome on or off: greet new members\n/setwelcome text: set the message (or send a photo with it)\n/resetwelcome: back to default\n/goodbye, /setgoodbye, /resetgoodbye: same for leavers\n/cleanwelcome on: delete the old welcome\n/welcomehelp: all fillings, random replies and buttons": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\nNew members are muted the moment they join. They must prove they are human before they can chat. Bots and spammers usually fail, so they never reach your members.\n\n<b>Turn it on</b>\n/welcome on first, then /captcha on. /captcha alone shows your current settings.\n\n<b>Modes</b> (/captchamode)\nbutton: tap one button. Easiest for members.\nmath: answer a sum like 4 + 7 = ?\ntext: type a short code shown in the message.\n\n<b>Time limits</b>\n/captchakicktime 5m: how long they have to verify.\n/captchakick on: remove people who do not verify (they can join again later).\n/captchamutetime 1h: keep them muted for a while after verifying. 0 means no extra mute.\nTimes use s, m, h, d, w (example 30m, 2h).\n\n<b>Custom button text</b>\n/setcaptchatext I am real: changes the button label.\n/resetcaptchatext: back to the default.\n\nAdmins and approved members skip the captcha.": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\nKeeps your group tidy by deleting messages the bot does not need you to see.\n\n<b>Clean commands</b>\nDeletes the command message itself a few seconds after it runs, so /warn or /ban do not fill the chat.\n/cleancommand all: clean every type\n/cleancommand admin: only commands sent by admins\n/cleancommand user: only commands sent by members\n/cleancommand other: commands aimed at other bots\n/keepcommand user: stop cleaning that type\n/cleancommand alone shows what is on.\n\n<b>Clean service messages</b>\nService messages are the grey lines Telegram adds, like Asha joined or Raj pinned a message.\n/cleanservice join: delete joined lines\n/cleanservice leave: delete left lines\nOther types: photo, pin, title, videochat, other, all.\n/keepservice or /nocleanservice: stop cleaning a type\n/cleanservicetypes: what each type means\n\nExample: /cleanservice join leave": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\nStops members from using a command in your group, without removing the bot feature for other groups.\n\n/disable rob: members can no longer use /rob here\n/enable rob: allow it again\n/disabled: list what is disabled\n/disableable: commands that can never be disabled\n\n<b>Options</b>\n/disabledel on: also delete the blocked command message\n/disableadmin on: block admins too (off by default)\n\nExample: /disable spin": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\nSends a record of every ban, mute, kick and warn to a private channel, so your team can review them.\n\n<b>Set up</b>\n1. Create a channel and add Rumi as admin.\n2. In your group send /setlog -100123456789 (the channel id).\n3. Rumi posts a test line to confirm.\n\n/logchannel: show the link and what is off\n/unsetlog: remove the link\n/nolog warn: stop logging one category\n/log warn: log it again\n/logcategories: ban, mute, kick, warn, lock, blocklist, flood, settings": "",
"<b>/anonadmin on</b>\nAdmins who post as the group (anonymous) can use admin commands. Off by default for safety.\n\n<b>/silentactions on</b>\nHides ban, mute and warn notices from the group. Admins still see them in the log channel, so link one with /setlog first.\n\n<b>/adminerror on or off</b>\nWhether members get a reply when they try an admin command. (Setting is saved; full effect comes in a later update.)": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\n<blockquote>Notes are saved messages your group can read any time. Great for rules, links, FAQs and group info. Admins save them, everyone can read them.</blockquote>\n\n<b>Commands</b>\n/save name text: save a note. You can also reply to any message (text, photo, video, sticker, voice, file) with /save name and Rumi keeps it.\n/get name: show a note. Add noformat to see the raw text with all the codes, like /get rules noformat\n#name: typing #rules in the chat works exactly like /get rules\n/notes: list every note in this group\n/clear name: delete one note\n/clearallnotes: delete all notes\n/privatenotes on or off: when on, a note shows an Open note button and members read it in a private chat with Rumi, so the group stays clean\n\n<b>Example</b>\n<blockquote>/save rules Hi {first}, be kind and no spam</blockquote>\nMembers type #rules and see: Hi Aarav, be kind and no spam\n\n<b>Fillings</b> (replaced for each reader)\n{first} first name, {last} last name, {fullname} both, {username} username, {mention} a tap-to-open name, {id} user id, {chatname} group name\n\n<b>Random replies</b>\nPut %%% between answers and Rumi picks one each time.\nExample: /save hello Hey there %%% Hi hi %%% Welcome in\n\n<b>Buttons</b>\nAdd a link button with [Text](buttonurl://https://example.com)\nAdd :same to put it on the same row as the one before: [Text](buttonurl://https://example.com:same)\nColours: add :blue, :green or :red\nA button can also open another note: [Rules](buttonurl://#rules)\n\n<b>Special tags</b> (put them anywhere in the note)\n{private}: this note always opens in private\n{noprivate}: this note always shows in the group\n{admin}: only admins can read this note\n{nonotif}: send without a sound\n{protect}: stop forwarding and saving\n{mediaspoiler}: hide photos and videos behind a spoiler": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\n<blockquote>A filter is an automatic reply. When someone writes a trigger word, Rumi answers on its own. Great for greetings, FAQs and common questions.</blockquote>\n\n<b>Commands</b>\n/filter word reply: set an automatic reply. You can also reply to a photo, video, sticker or file with /filter word\n/filters: list every filter in this group\n/stop word: remove one filter\n/clearfilters: remove all filters\n\n<b>Example</b>\n<blockquote>/filter price Our plans start at 99 rupees</blockquote>\nNow when anyone writes the word price anywhere in a message, Rumi sends that reply.\n\n<b>Trigger options</b> (put these in front of the word)\nexact:word : Rumi replies only when the whole message is exactly that word.\nExample: /filter exact:hi Hello there\nprefix:word : Rumi replies when the message starts with that word.\nExample: /filter prefix:good Have a great day\nWith no option, Rumi replies when the word appears anywhere as a whole word.\n\n<b>Fillings</b> (replaced for each person)\n{first} first name, {last} last name, {fullname} both, {username} username, {mention} a tap-to-open name, {id} user id, {chatname} group name\nExample: /filter hello Hey {first}, welcome to {chatname}\n\n<b>Random replies</b>\nPut %%% between answers and Rumi picks one each time.\nExample: /filter gm Good morning %%% Gm gm %%% Rise and shine\n\n<b>Buttons</b>\nAdd a link button with [Text](buttonurl://https://example.com)\nAdd :same to share a row, and :blue, :green or :red for colours.\nA button can also open a saved note: [Rules](buttonurl://#rules)\n\n<b>Other tags</b>\n{nonotif}: send without a sound\n{protect}: stop forwarding and saving\n{mediaspoiler}: hide photos and videos behind a spoiler\n\n<b>What members see</b>\nMembers just write a message. Rumi replies to it with your saved answer. They never need a command.": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\n<blockquote>Saves all of this group's Rumi settings into one small file, so you can restore them later or copy them to another group. Perfect when you set up a group carefully and never want to redo it 💫</blockquote>\n\n<b>What is saved</b>\nNotes, filters, rules, locks, blocklist, allowlist, welcome and goodbye texts, captcha, antiflood, antiraid, report, pin, cleaning, disabled commands, log channel, warn settings and other group settings.\n\n<b>What is never touched</b>\nWallets, coins, ranks, warns of members, approved members, AFK and anything personal. Backups only hold group settings.\n\n<b>Commands</b>\n/export: sends you the backup file. Any admin can use it.\n/import: loads a backup file into this group. Only the group creator can use it.\n/reset: clears all Rumi settings of this group. Only the group creator can use it, and it asks to confirm first.\n\n<b>How to export</b>\nType /export in your group. Rumi sends a file named like rumi_backup_12345.json. Keep it safe, it is your backup.\n\n<b>How to import</b>\n1. Send the backup file into the group you want to fill.\n2. Reply to that file with /import\n3. Rumi loads everything and tells you how many entries were added.\nImportant: import replaces the settings of the sections found in the file. Anything in those sections that is not in the file is removed. If something goes wrong, nothing is changed.\n\n<b>How to reset</b>\nType /reset. Rumi shows two buttons: Yes, reset and Cancel. Only the group creator can press them. After Yes, every setting listed above is wiped and the group starts fresh.\n\n<b>Example</b>\n<blockquote>Group A is perfect. In group A: /export\nOpen group B, forward the file there, reply to it with /import\nGroup B now has the same notes, filters and rules ✨</blockquote>\n\n<b>What members see</b>\nMembers see nothing special. Only admins and the creator use these commands. If a normal member tries, Rumi politely says it is for admins or the creator only.\n\n<b>Good to know</b>\nActive raid timers and the last welcome message are not saved on purpose, so an old raid mode never comes back by mistake.\n": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\n<blockquote>Topics split one big group into neat rooms, like Memes, Music or Support. These commands let admins create and manage those rooms without opening group settings 💫</blockquote>\n\n<b>Before you start</b>\n1. Turn on Topics in your group settings (the group must be a supergroup).\n2. Make Rumi an admin with the Manage Topics right.\n\n<b>Commands</b>\n/newtopic name: creates a new topic.\n/renametopic name: renames the topic you are standing in.\n/closetopic: closes the current topic, so only admins can write there.\n/reopentopic: opens a closed topic again for everyone.\n/deletetopic: deletes the current topic and everything inside it.\n\n<b>Examples</b>\n<blockquote>/newtopic Memes and fun\nRumi creates a topic called Memes and fun.\n\nInside that topic:\n/renametopic Chill zone\n/closetopic\n/reopentopic</blockquote>\n\n<b>Good to know</b>\n/renametopic, /closetopic, /reopentopic and /deletetopic must be sent inside the topic you want to change. /newtopic can be sent anywhere in the group.\n/deletetopic cannot be undone, so use it carefully.\n\n<b>What members see</b>\nMembers only see the result: a new room appears, a name changes, or a room becomes read-only. If a normal member tries these commands, Rumi politely says they are for admins only.\n\n<b>If something fails</b>\nMost of the time it means Rumi is missing the Manage Topics right, or the group does not have Topics turned on. Fix that and try again ✨\n": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\n<blockquote>Links your private chat with Rumi to one of your groups. It is the first step to managing a group from your DM, without cluttering the group chat 💫</blockquote>\n\n<b>Commands</b>\n/connect group_id: links you to a group. You must be an admin there, and Rumi must be inside it.\n/connection: shows which group you are linked to right now.\n/disconnect: removes the link.\n/reconnect: shows a button to link your last group again in one tap.\n\n<b>All of these are used in a private chat with Rumi, not inside the group.</b>\n\n<b>How to find the group id</b>\nAdd me to the group, then ask an admin to send /id there. Copy the number. It usually starts with -100.\n\n<b>Example</b>\n<blockquote>In my private chat with Rumi:\n/connect -1001234567890\nRumi answers: you are linked to My Group.\n\nLater:\n/connection shows the linked group\n/disconnect removes the link\n/reconnect brings it back with one tap ✨</blockquote>\n\n<b>Good to know</b>\nYou can be linked to one group at a time. Connecting to another group replaces the old link.\nOnly admins of that group can connect to it, so nobody can link themselves to a group they do not manage.\n\n<b>What members see</b>\nNothing. Connections happen privately in your DM, so the group stays clean.\n\n<b>Coming next</b>\nOnce linked, more group commands will be usable from your DM. For now the link is saved and ready ✨\n": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\n<blockquote>Lets every member pick the language Rumi uses with them. Right now English and Hindi are available, and more languages will come later 💫</blockquote>\n\n<b>Command</b>\n/setlang: shows language buttons. Tap the one you like and Rumi saves it.\n\n<b>Example</b>\n<blockquote>/setlang\nRumi shows: English and Hindi buttons.\nTap Hindi, and Rumi confirms in Hindi ✨</blockquote>\n\n<b>Good to know</b>\nYour choice is personal. It is saved only for you, so a friend in the same group can use a different language.\nYou can change it any time by sending /setlang again.\nAt the moment the language applies to the language menu itself. Other Rumi messages will be translated step by step in future updates.\n\n<b>What members see</b>\nTwo buttons and a short confirmation message. Nothing else changes in the group.\n": "",
"<b>What it does</b>\n<blockquote>Small helpful commands that anyone can use. No setup needed, just type them 💫</blockquote>\n\n<b>Commands</b>\n/runs: Rumi shows a playful message about you running away. Just for fun.\n/limits: shows Telegram's limits for message length, captions, buttons and note names. Handy when a long note fails to send.\n/privacy: explains what Rumi keeps so its features can work, and what it never asks for.\n/markdownhelp: shows the text tags Rumi understands in notes, filters and welcome texts, like bold, italic, spoiler and links.\n/donate: tells you the best way to support Rumi.\n\n<b>Example</b>\n<blockquote>/limits\nRumi lists: a text message holds up to 4096 characters, a caption up to 1024, and a message can carry up to 100 buttons ✨</blockquote>\n\n<b>Good to know</b>\nThese commands work in groups and in private chat.\n/markdownhelp is a quick reminder. The full guide, with fillings and buttons, is in the Notes page of /help.\n\n<b>What members see</b>\nA short, friendly message with a quote box. Nothing is saved or changed.\n": "",
